    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Every triangle has exactly one circle that\ntouches all three sides: its incircle.\n\nThe green lines are the angle bisectors. They\nalways meet in a single point, the incenter\n(gray) - the center of the incircle. A\nperpendicular from the incenter to a side\ngives the green point where the circle\ntouches.\n\nDrag the yellow vertices: the circle always\nfits." DecimalsToShow="2" X="7.758" Y="-6.635" />
